#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eee2e26-910b-54d7-968a-9e9289a5225f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724826} {:answer/id #uuid "3f6f3331-a39d-5288-9d3c-d1553b1ed810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724835} {:answer/id #uuid "77e2e752-d9d1-5ac5-99e8-d03475c23abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724843} {:answer/id #uuid "d8278e0c-9b90-54e4-a206-e6700d5c70af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724853} {:answer/id #uuid "f3dcbe36-e94a-5008-acb1-c65178b5ba5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724858}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724835} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabd5c35-96ec-5225-9f03-6f8a8cc8a69a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2f7710e7-ac38-5419-8d46-a799d8583e60" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the following lines.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=3 x + 1,\\qquad y=3 x - 1, \\\\ x&=y - 1,\\qquad x=y + 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1: Choose coordinates.** Rewrite each boundary using its shared expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 x - y&=-1,\\qquad 3 x - y=1, \\\\ x - y&=-1,\\qquad x - y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nChoose $u=3 x - y$ and $v=x - y$.\n\n**Step 2: Map the boundaries.** The four boundaries become $u=-1$, $u=1$, $v=-1$, and $v=4$. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):-1\\leq u\\leq 1,\\ -1\\leq v\\leq 4\\}.\n$$\n\n![The transformed rectangle.](images/66/666f6d0c04138db1649106b89e6383d1e2860dcde88e6dd25c5413612af5e704.png)\n\n**Step 3: Compute the forward Jacobian.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}3&-1 \\\\ 1&-1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4: Take the reciprocal and its magnitude.** The inverse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{u}{2} - \\frac{v}{2}, \\\\ y&=\\frac{u}{2} - \\frac{3 v}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant is nonzero, so this linear inverse is defined everywhere. Area uses the absolute value of the reciprocal determinant:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{1}{-2}\\right|=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5: Integrate over the rectangle.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Area}(D)&=\\iint_{\\Delta}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{-1}^{4}\\int_{-1}^{1}1\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\left(1-(-1)\\right)\\cdot\\left(4-(-1)\\right) \\\\ &=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "280fea5c-2840-5a46-b937-958ec1da35f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724829} {:answer/id #uuid "3d262065-73ee-51b5-a568-b317830482f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724834} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f32477-a26e-5e02-9ac8-a617af66fb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724847} {:answer/id #uuid "b3fee6c1-2f18-5c56-be3a-41d62d6da84d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724849} {:answer/id #uuid "b6900d62-3f41-5051-8cf6-381c422c749b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724850}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724849} :answer-field/id #uuid "68b27c23-e5b1-5b02-8113-e11b60afc42b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a8cff10-0eeb-507e-8afa-7eee09930a4f" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the following lines.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 y&=5 x - 3,\\qquad 3 y=5 x - 8, \\\\ 4 x&=2 y - 1,\\qquad 4 x=2 y + 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1: Choose coordinates.** Rewrite each boundary using its shared expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 x - 3 y&=3,\\qquad 5 x - 3 y=8, \\\\ 4 x - 2 y&=-1,\\qquad 4 x - 2 y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nChoose $u=5 x - 3 y$ and $v=4 x - 2 y$.\n\n**Step 2: Map the boundaries.** The four boundaries become $u=3$, $u=8$, $v=-1$, and $v=4$. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):3\\leq u\\leq 8,\\ -1\\leq v\\leq 4\\}.\n$$\n\n![The transformed rectangle.](images/7d/7d3a235807027c0a82f61ae54f940338b435b929976f8de871e226e25f52a600.png)\n\n**Step 3: Compute the forward Jacobian.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}5&-3 \\\\ 4&-2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4: Take the reciprocal and its magnitude.** The inverse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=- u + \\frac{3 v}{2}, \\\\ y&=- 2 u + \\frac{5 v}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant is nonzero, so this linear inverse is defined everywhere. Area uses the absolute value of the reciprocal determinant:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right|=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5: Integrate over the rectangle.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Area}(D)&=\\iint_{\\Delta}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{-1}^{4}\\int_{3}^{8}1\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\left(8-(3)\\right)\\cdot\\left(4-(-1)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{25}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1958bc17-ed08-5a8b-abf5-8c05dae0ebf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724828} {:answer/id #uuid "40228f3f-f5cf-5569-b28c-a49f6ac533b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724836} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfeade5-74b7-5a4f-ad0f-69216c0fa4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724844} {:answer/id #uuid "b315406e-749b-57f3-b155-1e85d0e4f6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724848} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c68967-7bda-5b14-9035-1976daea5372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724851}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724836} :answer-field/id #uuid "07446a4d-823f-58e9-bdd5-8254d40acf02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55425c9f-a613-5cc1-a134-bac67eefc04c" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the following lines.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 y&=3 x - 3,\\qquad 2 y=3 x - 8, \\\\ 2 x&=3 y - 3,\\qquad 2 x=3 y - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1: Choose coordinates.** Rewrite each boundary using its shared expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 x - 2 y&=3,\\qquad 3 x - 2 y=8, \\\\ 2 x - 3 y&=-3,\\qquad 2 x - 3 y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nChoose $u=3 x - 2 y$ and $v=2 x - 3 y$.\n\n**Step 2: Map the boundaries.** The four boundaries become $u=3$, $u=8$, $v=-3$, and $v=-2$. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):3\\leq u\\leq 8,\\ -3\\leq v\\leq -2\\}.\n$$\n\n![The transformed rectangle.](images/09/0959b84849d391c6f3eb3e9ae73157d5ee65a51030233441533acdde2eace96e.png)\n\n**Step 3: Compute the forward Jacobian.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}3&-2 \\\\ 2&-3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4: Take the reciprocal and its magnitude.** The inverse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{3 u}{5} - \\frac{2 v}{5}, \\\\ y&=\\frac{2 u}{5} - \\frac{3 v}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant is nonzero, so this linear inverse is defined everywhere. Area uses the absolute value of the reciprocal determinant:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{1}{-5}\\right|=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5: Integrate over the rectangle.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Area}(D)&=\\iint_{\\Delta}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{5}\\int_{-3}^{-2}\\int_{3}^{8}1\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot\\left(8-(3)\\right)\\cdot\\left(-2-(-3)\\right) \\\\ &=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5a11a7-b0d4-59e5-8e86-9cfad9c3cd65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724830} {:answer/id #uuid "321dc4dd-e7a4-5b79-9241-664fd435284a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724832} {:answer/id #uuid "48e6d8e8-dac4-5646-9cd7-e81a38e5adb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724837} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d3b101-fb00-5898-92e7-c7f261a42065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724855} {:answer/id #uuid "ecdec577-6a9b-52d9-8d17-32c12fad0160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724857}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724830} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e313794-1492-5357-ab04-12ad46ddea39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5dfcfe54-7c72-53f3-b1aa-b710ece810dd" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the following lines.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=2 x - 1,\\qquad y=2 x - 5, \\\\ x&=2 y + 3,\\qquad x=2 y + 7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1: Choose coordinates.** Rewrite each boundary using its shared expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 x - y&=1,\\qquad 2 x - y=5, \\\\ x - 2 y&=3,\\qquad x - 2 y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nChoose $u=2 x - y$ and $v=x - 2 y$.\n\n**Step 2: Map the boundaries.** The four boundaries become $u=1$, $u=5$, $v=3$, and $v=7$. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):1\\leq u\\leq 5,\\ 3\\leq v\\leq 7\\}.\n$$\n\n![The transformed rectangle.](images/15/154c9ec2df4b1498040f6230c4eb999be5c4bddf3fda5225a63383cbd94f52c2.png)\n\n**Step 3: Compute the forward Jacobian.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}2&-1 \\\\ 1&-2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4: Take the reciprocal and its magnitude.** The inverse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{2 u}{3} - \\frac{v}{3}, \\\\ y&=\\frac{u}{3} - \\frac{2 v}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant is nonzero, so this linear inverse is defined everywhere. Area uses the absolute value of the reciprocal determinant:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{1}{-3}\\right|=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5: Integrate over the rectangle.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Area}(D)&=\\iint_{\\Delta}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{3}^{7}\\int_{1}^{5}1\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\left(5-(1)\\right)\\cdot\\left(7-(3)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171927ac-5106-5b59-9c2f-1a80e132140f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724827} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab9917e-4ca0-5e35-879e-163d68b0e727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724833} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddeeedb-3dbd-5f1b-bf7d-9ec7dbdcf764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724840} {:answer/id #uuid "8e79469b-626e-5f0b-89b5-99194ef9e7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724845} {:answer/id #uuid "daff6da4-48e6-54c4-836d-54c27e813c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186724845} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc32484a-fca6-56c6-acb3-173db1ff7ce0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186724859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eaeed937-6b20-571c-9866-ea11785bebbe" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the following lines.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=3 x - 3,\\qquad y=3 x - 4, \\\\ x&=3 y - 2,\\qquad x=3 y - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1: Choose coordinates.** Rewrite each boundary using its shared expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 x - y&=3,\\qquad 3 x - y=4, \\\\ x - 3 y&=-2,\\qquad x - 3 y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nChoose $u=3 x - y$ and $v=x - 3 y$.\n\n**Step 2: Map the boundaries.** The four boundaries become $u=3$, $u=4$, $v=-2$, and $v=-1$. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):3\\leq u\\leq 4,\\ -2\\leq v\\leq -1\\}.\n$$\n\n![The transformed rectangle.](images/31/31a33026b52241892a59844eb75067f8fa4c5fc47e17054cf31d358ccdb9cb7a.png)\n\n**Step 3: Compute the forward Jacobian.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}3&-1 \\\\ 1&-3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4: Take the reciprocal and its magnitude.** The inverse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{3 u}{8} - \\frac{v}{8}, \\\\ y&=\\frac{u}{8} - \\frac{3 v}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant is nonzero, so this linear inverse is defined everywhere. Area uses the absolute value of the reciprocal determinant:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{1}{-8}\\right|=\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5: Integrate over the rectangle.**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Area}(D)&=\\iint_{\\Delta}\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{8}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{3}^{4}1\\,\\mathrm du\\,\\mathrm dv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot\\left(4-(3)\\right)\\cdot\\left(-1-(-2)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
